---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const VERSION = '0.6.0';
const BASE = `https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-app/releases/download/v${VERSION}`;

const BUILDS = [
  { file: `lumen-${VERSION}-arm64-v8a.apk`, label: 'arm64-v8a', size: '21.1 MB', note: 'Most phones from the last several years. Recommended.' },
  { file: `lumen-${VERSION}-armeabi-v7a.apk`, label: 'armeabi-v7a', size: '17.4 MB', note: 'Older 32-bit ARM phones.' },
  { file: `lumen-${VERSION}-x86_64.apk`, label: 'x86_64', size: '23.0 MB', note: 'Emulators and x86 devices.' },
  { file: `lumen-${VERSION}-universal.apk`, label: 'Universal', size: '60.3 MB', note: 'Any supported device, in a much larger file.' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Download"
  description="Download the signed Lumen Android APK, with checksums and installation steps."
>
  <div class="hero page-hero">
    <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
    <h1 class="hero-enter">Lumen for Android</h1>
    <p class="lead hero-enter" style="animation-delay: 160ms">
      Version {VERSION}. Signed APK, Android 7.0 or newer, English interface. Not on Google Play.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row hero-enter" style="animation-delay: 300ms">
      <a class="button primary" href={`${BASE}/lumen-${VERSION}-arm64-v8a.apk`}>Download for most phones (arm64)</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={`https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-app/releases/tag/v${VERSION}`}>All files and release notes</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Builds</p>
      <h2>Pick the file for your phone</h2>
      <p>If you are not sure, take the arm64 build. If it does not install, try the universal one.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="status-grid">
      {BUILDS.map((build) => (
        <div class="status-card">
          <h3>{build.label}</h3>
          <p>{build.note}</p>
          <p><a href={`${BASE}/${build.file}`}>{build.file}</a> ({build.size})</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
      <h2>Three steps</h2>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li>Download the APK on the phone.</li>
      <li>Open it and, when Android asks, allow installs from your browser or file manager.</li>
      <li>Open Lumen and answer the five first-launch questions.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Verify</p>
      <h2>Check what you downloaded</h2>
      <p>
        Every release has a <a href={`${BASE}/SHA256SUMS.txt`}>SHA256SUMS.txt</a> file. On a computer,
        put it next to the APK and run:
      </p>
    </div>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt --ignore-missing</code></pre>
    <p>The APKs are signed with the project key. Its certificate SHA-256 fingerprint is:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>AC:8B:8C:33:5D:06:BA:82:AE:5B:62:97:0B:C6:5F:A5:60:03:23:D1:11:8E:97:A2:0F:4D:E8:38:D8:1F:84:96</code></pre>
    <p>Compare it with the output of <code>apksigner verify --print-certs</code> on the file.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="status-grid">
      <div class="status-card">
        <h3>What this build does</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Onboarding, adaptive interface, and settings</li>
          <li>A screen for each of the eight modules, running real logic</li>
          <li>Profile, enabled modules and data kept between launches, in an encrypted on-device database</li>
          <li>Speaks phrases and flashcards aloud, and vibrates for sound alerts</li>
          <li>Optional live accelerometer for fall detection and gait monitoring</li>
          <li>Works with no internet connection</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="status-card pending">
        <h3>What it does not do yet</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Camera and microphone input: Vision and Hearing work on typed or sample input</li>
          <li>Real SMS: SOS uses a fake sender and can never send a message</li>
          <li>Reminder notifications</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem">
      This build was tested in an Android 15 emulator, not on a physical phone, and has had no screen
      reader testing. If you installed 0.5.0, uninstall it first: that version crashed on launch. Lumen helps but does not replace a doctor or the emergency
      number, and it is not a certified medical device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">From source</p>
      <h2>Build it yourself</h2>
      <p>
        With the <a href="https://docs.flutter.dev/get-started/install">Flutter SDK</a>, the Android SDK and
        a JDK 17 installed:
      </p>
    </div>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>git clone https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-app.git
cd lumen-app
flutter pub get
flutter build apk --release --split-per-abi</code></pre>
    <p>
      The <a href="/docs/getting-started/running-the-app/">running the app</a> page covers running it on a device or
      emulator, and the <a href="/docs/contributing/release-process/">release process</a> explains signing.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-app">lumen-app on GitHub</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/demo/">Try the browser demo</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
